,["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Hardy-Weinberg"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"Allele frequency equilibrium"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"Calculate expected random-mating genotype proportions, then apply selection, one-way mutation, or migration to track how allele frequency p changes. Genetic drift is explored in its own lab."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Genetic Drift","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-rose-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-500 to-pink-600 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"🎲"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Genetic Drift"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"Random allele change in small populations"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"50/50 starting alleles, no selection — just random sampling. Smaller populations show larger fluctuations; larger populations usually stay closer to 50/50. Connects repeated drift to founder effects and bottlenecks."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Common Ancestry","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-yellow-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-yellow-500 to-amber-600 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"🦴"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Common Ancestry"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"Homologous bones across species"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"Click any bone in the human arm — see the same bone in a bat wing, whale flipper, horse leg, and bird wing. Same skeleton, different jobs. Then sort fifteen real findings into the five lines of evidence."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Antibiotic Resistance","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-fuchsia-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-fuchsia-500 to-pink-700 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"💊"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Antibiotic Resistance"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"Watch bacteria evolve resistance"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"Apply antibiotic pulses to a simplified bacterial population and observe selection on resistance. In real life, use antibiotics only when needed and take them exactly as prescribed."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Coevolution Lab","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-red-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-red-500 to-orange-700 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"🐆"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Coevolution Lab"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"Predator-prey arms race"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"Two populations evolving against each other. Predators get faster; prey escape better; the cycle continues. Demonstrates the Red Queen hypothesis: you have to keep running just to stay in place."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Discovery Timeline","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-stone-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-stone-500 to-stone-700 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"📜"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Discovery Timeline"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"How we learned what we know"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"The 290-year history of evolution science: Darwin, Wallace, Mendel, the Modern Synthesis, the often-overlooked figures (Margulis, Franklin, McClintock), and the field and lab studies that watched selection happen (Kettlewell, the Grants, Lenski)."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Misconceptions Quiz","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-slate-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-500 to-slate-700 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"❓"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Misconceptions Quiz"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"12 common evolution errors"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"Targets the misunderstandings: \"just a theory,\" \"humans from monkeys,\" evolution-with-a-goal, survival-of-the-strongest. Each question gives a detailed evidence-based correction."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Selection Sleuth","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-amber-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-500 to-orange-700 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"🕵️"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Selection Sleuth"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"10 vignettes — name the mechanism"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"For each scenario, identify the evolutionary mechanism: natural selection (directional / stabilizing / disruptive), sexual selection, artificial selection, or genetic drift. Forces students past \"evolution = natural selection\" toward the full taxonomy of mechanisms."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Homology vs Analogy","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-cyan-500/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-cyan-500 to-blue-700 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"🦴"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Homology vs Analogy"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"10 trait pairs — same origin or same function"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"For each pair of structures, decide: homologous (same evolutionary origin, often different function — like human arm vs whale flipper) or analogous (same function, different origin — like bird wing vs butterfly wing). The signature distinction for inferring common descent."]]],["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Capstone Project","class":"relative text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 overflow-hidden group focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 ring-emerald-700/40"},["DIV",{"class":"bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-700 to-cyan-800 p-5 text-white"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between mb-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-4xl"},"🎓"],["SPAN",{"class":"bg-white/20 backdrop-blur px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"},"Mini"]],["H2",{"class":"text-xl font-black"},"Capstone Project"],["P",{"class":"text-sm opacity-90 font-medium"},"Predict, test, explain"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5"},["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed "},"A guided investigation with a persistent evidence notebook. Pick a real-world scenario, predict the outcome, test it in a linked simulation, record data, and generate a print-ready lab report."]]]]]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-8 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-600 mb-2 px-1 flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{},"Teacher Resources"],["SPAN",{"class":"normal-case font-medium text-slate-600"},"— for educators planning a unit"]],["DIV",{"class":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4"},["BUTTON",{"aria-label":"Class Snapshot — paste student journals to see completion, prediction hit rates, misconceptions, and field notes","class":"text-left bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all border-2 border-amber-300 hover:border-amber-500 overflow-hidden focus:ou